1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:02,880
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,797
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,437
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:10,696
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,195
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:13,640
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:16,860
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,260
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,437
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,617
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,820
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:35,380
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:40,640
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:42,880
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:52,777
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:55,497
Your heart will be your guide.

17
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:58,697
Raise the sails and take the helm!

18
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:01,337
That legendary place?

19
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:04,077
That the end of the map reveals.

20
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,957
Is only legendary.

21
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:10,317
Until someone proves it real!

22
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,657
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times!

23
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:17,037
Through the heartache
and through the pain!

24
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:21,497
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:24,500
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:28,437
So come aboard and bring along!

27
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:30,840
All your hopes and dreams.

28
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:34,077
Together we will find everything!

29
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,240
That we're looking for.

30
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,877
There's always room for you.

31
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:42,660
If you wanna be my friend?

32
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:47,080
We are, we are on the cruise.

33
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:49,940
We are.

34
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:52,470
Huh?

35
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,700
Captain Smoker!

36
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:59,337
A message from headquarters!

37
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:01,277
I've just received word that Monkey D.

38
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:04,537
Luffy and his pirate crew are headed
to Log Town from the East Blue.

39
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:08,502
The bounty on his head has just
been raised to 30 million berries!

40
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,780
30 million berries.

41
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:14,080
I can't wait to congratulate him.

42
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:18,077
Sir, this is the pirate that defeated
Don Creek and destroyed Arlong Park!

43
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,200
Shut your mouth.

44
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:28,540
All your whining made
it collapse in defeat.

45
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,480
I'm sorry, sir. Silence.

46
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:32,240
Your stress is useless.

47
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:35,231
You alone dictate the pace of your battle.

48
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,420
Am I wrong?

49
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,160
No, sir.

50
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,080
Then why so tense?

51
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:45,760
Uh, well,

52
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:49,337
it's been a long time since I faced a
pirate group of this considerable strength,

53
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,250
sir.

54
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:53,657
You really have nothing to worry
about under my command has there been

55
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:59,300
even a single pirate to set foot on this
island without being captured No, sir,

56
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,220
just calm the hell down.

57
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,499
You're screwing up my pacing marine

58
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:09,577
Reporting sir, I have word that a
pirate group has recently arrived.

59
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:12,980
You're requested there at
once It must be Luffy's group.

60
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:14,137
How'd they do that?

61
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:16,480
I just got this 30 million, huh?

62
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:18,920
This might actually be interesting

63
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,450
Sir?

64
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:22,960
Just talking to myself, forget it.

65
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:27,458
Don't you want to see this, Captain?

66
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:33,977
Captain, you have to tell
us what your orders are.

67
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:34,900
No need to.

68
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:38,182
Sir, do you even know who
this pirate's defeated?

69
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,101
Where's Toshiki?

70
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,957
Sir, she mentioned to me that she
had some things to do this morning,

71
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:47,334
but that she tried to make
it back in time for training.

72
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,777
Irresponsible, girl.

73
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:50,057
Where the hell's she go?

74
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:50,970
Yay!

75
00:03:51,053 --> 00:03:51,941
I got ice cream!

76
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:55,536
You better slow it down or
you're gonna drop it, okay?

77
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:05,020
Captain Smoker!

78
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:06,560
My ice cream!

79
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:09,680
I am very sorry, sir!
Please don't hurt her!

80
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:10,837
My daughter shouldn't run!

81
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:11,750
Please don't hurt me!

82
00:04:11,833 --> 00:04:12,663
I'm sorry!

83
00:04:12,746 --> 00:04:13,715
Please don't hurt us!

84
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:15,480
I'm sorry.

85
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:18,407
My silly pants have
eaten all your ice cream.

86
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:21,000
Here, go buy yourself five scoops.

87
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,200
Let's go. Sir!

88
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,940
Thank you, sir! Thank you!

89
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,700
Have at it, boys!

90
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:38,677
No need to be shy on my
account! I, Call the Crescent,

91
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:42,977
hereby proclaim all of your food to be at
service to the future King of the Pirates!

92
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:45,597
So don't bother trying to hide anything.

93
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:46,780
Hey?

94
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,380
Who's in charge here?

95
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:53,260
I think you need to
leave So you're Monkey D.

96
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:54,330
Luffy

97
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,537
You're not worth 30 million.

98
00:04:56,620 --> 00:05:00,557
I guess you're not worth much more
than my grandma's false teeth.

99
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,837
Don't you dare speak to me that way!

100
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:03,780
Got it?

101
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:14,820
Captain Smoker?

102
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:18,897
He is definitely one of the toughest
Marines we've ever seen in this town.

103
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:22,457
See, Log Town used to be a hangout
for pirates headed to the Grand Line,

104
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:23,437
but not anymore.

105
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,957
As soon as Smoker took over,

106
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:28,497
any pirate that's ever come near this
island has been caught, incarcerated,

107
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,410
and executed.

108
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:30,820
Smoker is bad.

109
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,300
He's a complete and utter monster.

110
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:37,155
There are even those who say
he has Devil Fruit powers.

111
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:40,100
Devil Fruit powers?

112
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:48,500
That's amazing, Captain.

113
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:50,777
You captured Luffy all by yourself.

114
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:52,272
You're a complete idiot.

115
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:53,417
This isn't Luffy.

116
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:55,260
Anyone could tell that. Huh?

117
00:05:55,580 --> 00:05:59,160
If this garbage was worth 30
million, I'd become a pirate.

118
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:01,000
So then where's Luffy?

119
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:02,534
And what's your hurry?

120
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:05,200
He'll be here soon enough.

121
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:06,580
I'm here.

122
00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:09,940
But where's the execution platform?

123
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,440
This looks like the docks. Hey!

124
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,741
Can you help me?

125
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,860
Is he a member of this garbage?

126
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,340
No, I don't think so. Not him.

127
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:19,815
Hi, I need some help.

128
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:22,517
Do you happen to know where
they execute people around here?

129
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,237
The platform. Yeah, I know.

130
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,717
I just can't seem to find it.

131
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,460
I haven't seen you before.

132
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,477
This is my first time here on the island.

133
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,937
The town is a whole lot
bigger than Fuchsia Village,

134
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:34,737
and it's really spread out, too.

135
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,460
So why go to the platform?

136
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:37,780
Personal quest.

137
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:40,591
To see where the king of the pirates died.

138
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:46,940
I guess you don't know. Oh, well. Hold it.

139
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,920
Just follow the smoke, kid.

140
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:52,220
Great! That way?

141
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:53,558
I'll see you later!

142
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:14,157
this really sucks damn i just
want to find the execution

143
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:17,237
platform but somehow i keep
Getting myself turned around.

144
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:18,732
I'll find it eventually.

145
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,560
Let's see.

146
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:25,790
This way.

147
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:29,380
Gold Roger.

148
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:51,600
Excuse me, do you work here?

149
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:55,377
The sign hanging outside said this
place is called the Gold Roger.

150
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,813
How'd it get that name?

151
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,390
Scram.

152
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:00,100
You should leave.

153
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:03,006
This isn't a place for
unaccompanied children.

154
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:06,006
Besides, we're closed
for good starting today.

155
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:07,400
You're going under?

156
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,280
I'm not going under.

157
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:11,518
I've decided to shut it down myself.

158
00:08:11,740 --> 00:08:12,660
I'm retiring.

159
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:15,848
Sorry, I just wanted
to know about the name.

160
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:20,300
See, I'm looking for the
execution platform, but I'm lost.

161
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,229
Could you tell me the way?

162
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,500
What the heck is that?

163
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:28,017
Whoa, it's a huge skull!

164
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:29,420
That is so cool!

165
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:30,920
Killer Giant,

166
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:35,057
one of the most feared villains to ever
haunt the waters of the Grand Line.

167
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:39,375
He sent hundreds of pirates to their
deaths over the course of his life.

168
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:45,297
But it only took Gold Roger a single
blow to put the behemoth down for good.

169
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:46,780
Gold Roger killed him?

170
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,500
With lightning speed.

171
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:51,240
And here's the wound that did it.

172
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:55,600
Killer Giant was a terrible
waste of human flesh anyway,

173
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,177
but he proclaimed with his dying breath,!

174
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:01,060
Gold Roger, I take my hat off to you.

175
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:04,080
You will forever be the
king of the pirates.

176
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:06,290
Awesome!

177
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,380
Tell me more!

178
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:12,017
When I'd heard he'd conquered the
Grand Line, I wasn't surprised.

179
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:17,040
I was happy to hear that he was the one
who finally survived those evil seas, yeah.

180
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:22,540
On this day 22 years ago, Gold
Roger died on that platform.

181
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,429
And that's how it started.

182
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:26,557
That's when it all began.

183
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:31,420
The so-called Great Pirate Era, where
everyone with a boat claims to be a pirate.

184
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:33,816
But look around this once great town.

185
00:09:34,020 --> 00:09:37,337
I'll bet you won't be able to
find yourself a real pirate.

186
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:40,000
Nothing here but cowards and scum.

187
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:42,777
Men brave enough to
make the journey to the

188
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:45,117
Grand Line have all
disappeared from these waters.

189
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:49,357
There are no more true pirates
left, that's why I'm closing down!

190
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,320
I'm going to the Grand Line.

191
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:58,100
Hell yeah, Gold Roger's so cool, he's
exactly how a pirate's supposed to be!

192
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:03,300
That's why I'm here, to go to the Grand
Line, get my hands on the One Piece,

193
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:05,502
and then be king of the pirates.

194
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:13,460
Oh, those are some pretty big words.

195
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:16,593
Even more so because you're in this bar.

196
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,271
I only said what I meant.

197
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,700
Young man,

198
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,137
if there are still people
like you out there,

199
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:26,257
should I hold off on closing this place?

200
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:27,170
I don't know.

201
00:10:27,253 --> 00:10:28,277
It could just be me.

202
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,190
That's right.

203
00:10:29,273 --> 00:10:30,475
It could just be you.

204
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:33,241
In that case, let's have a drink.

205
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:36,284
I haven't been in this
good a mood in some time.

206
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:38,740
Um, I don't drink alcohol.

207
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,980
All right, then how about this?

208
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:45,261
Let's raise our glasses together.

209
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,840
To the eternal King of the Pirates.

210
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,520
Here's to the King of the Pirates.

211
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,640
Nice catch!

212
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,979
It's an elephant bluefin tuna fish!

213
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,330
That's right.

214
00:11:10,413 --> 00:11:12,797
It must have got mixed
in from the south blue.

215
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,780
I got it with pole and lime.

216
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:16,560
Just a pole and lime?

217
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:19,600
Blue fin tuna fish.

218
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,740
Okay, let's go. Lift it.

219
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:22,780
Right, right.

220
00:11:22,920 --> 00:11:24,320
Hey, hold on a second.

221
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,580
How much for it?

222
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:28,200
Sell the fish to me.

223
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:31,160
I got everything I need.

224
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:35,417
I'm completely prepared for
whatever the sea can throw at me.

225
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:38,794
There isn't anything Usopp
Brave Warrior can't face now.

226
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,120
Uh, wait a minute.

227
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:42,457
I think I'm forgetting
something important.

228
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:43,370
That's it.

229
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:45,437
A first-class sniper
like myself should really

230
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:47,837
have a top-shelf pair of
goggles to look through.

231
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:49,637
I'm gonna get the best pair I can find.

232
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:52,157
I don't care what they cost,
unless it's more than I can afford.

233
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,880
Super Goggles, here I come!

234
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:07,422
These are them.

235
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:08,410
These are the ones.

236
00:12:08,493 --> 00:12:09,323
They're perfect.

237
00:12:09,406 --> 00:12:10,236
Hey, lady!

238
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:11,816
Those are brand new.

239
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,457
They're the top-of-the-line
model from North Blue Company.

240
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:18,577
Oh, and the import ship I get them from
only stops here in port once a year.

241
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:20,357
Hey, don't you have any money?

242
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,637
What's wrong with you?

243
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:22,957
I can't just give these away.

244
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,557
No, I...

245
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:26,117
That's right, my backpack.

246
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,141
I'll take those.

247
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:29,580
Oh, excellent choice.

248
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:31,057
And what a cute little girl.

249
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:34,917
I happen to know that these are the only
goggles of their kind on the whole island.

250
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:35,830
No!

251
00:12:35,913 --> 00:12:38,560
Those are my goggles! Drop them!

252
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,940
You snooze, you lose, Grandpa!

253
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:49,220
Huh? Grandpa?

254
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:53,640
Little girl, stop right there!

255
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:57,057
There is no way you could
possibly think I'm an old man.

256
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,877
I'm more like an older brother, right?

257
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:01,020
Well, you smell like an old man.

258
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,100
I am not old!

259
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:03,437
Just give me back those goggles!

260
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,557
I found them first!

261
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:05,470
They're mine!

262
00:13:05,553 --> 00:13:06,383
They're mine!

263
00:13:06,466 --> 00:13:07,296
They're mine!

264
00:13:07,379 --> 00:13:08,209
Yeah?

265
00:13:08,292 --> 00:13:09,122
You better watch your mouth!

266
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,697
Because I'm friends with the Marines
and I'll get them to beat you up!

267
00:13:11,780 --> 00:13:13,500
The Marines? That's right.

268
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:16,737
And their captain is a close
personal friend of my family's.

269
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:18,157
He's kind of like my uncle.

270
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:21,460
Why, you little... Ha!

271
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:23,091
I'm a great captain, too!

272
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:25,857
Our Long Park was destroyed
by these two hands!

273
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:27,717
I was surrounded by hundreds of fishmen,

274
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:31,437
and the last thing they ever saw
was Captain Usopp the Incredible!

275
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:35,617
Doing such amazing and terrible things,
they were glad to quickly meet their end!

276
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:40,347
Now I have a bounty of 30 million berries
on my head so Marines don't scare me!

277
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:42,820
Oh, 30 million berries, huh?

278
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:44,180
That's right!

279
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:45,750
Papa!

280
00:13:45,833 --> 00:13:47,100
Don't call me Papa.

281
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:48,398
I'm not your daddy.

282
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:51,060
I bought a present for you.

283
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:53,480
Happy birthday, Papa!

284
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,380
Oh, my girl.

285
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:03,837
Carol, you are absolutely the most angelic
little girl a father could ask for.

286
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:05,540
I love you so much, Papa.

287
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:08,140
What's with that girl?

288
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:11,977
But, Papa,

289
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:16,097
that silly old man over there was being
mean and trying to jack your present!

290
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:17,010
Now, now.

291
00:14:17,093 --> 00:14:18,137
Don't say jack, dear.

292
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:19,102
It's not right.

293
00:14:19,260 --> 00:14:20,900
For a proper young girl.

294
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:27,535
Are you the gentleman that's been
bothering my adorable little daughter?

295
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:30,357
No, I just...

296
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,793
There's something else!

297
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,616
There's a bounty of 30 million bears.

298
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,680
Oh, a bounty worth 30 million, huh?

299
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,260
Let's take a look.

300
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:42,380
Oh, are those the new bad guys?

301
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:44,880
Yeah, I just picked them up today.

302
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:53,600
600, 1.3 mil, 700, 30
million, Monkey D. Luffy.

303
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:56,280
For a first bounty, that's impressive.

304
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,320
Where are you going?

305
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,240
OK, that's not me.

306
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:03,697
I'm not the guy in the poster.

307
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:06,017
I was just trying to
pretend to be a bad guy.

308
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:06,930
Bye bye now.

309
00:15:07,013 --> 00:15:10,700
I'm out of here! Bye! See ya! Crap!

310
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:12,630
That's you.

311
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,429
Okay, you caught me again.

312
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:18,457
But just try and lay a hand on
me and you'll see what happens.

313
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:22,057
My Captain Luffy won't sit idly by
and watch one of his crew in danger.

314
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:25,817
He's a cold-blooded soulless demon
from the very pits of hell itself.

315
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,959
You can't even imagine the
pain that he can inflict.

316
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,317
You've got your daughter to worry about.

317
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,040
Why risk your life over it?

318
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:33,970
You're right.

319
00:15:34,053 --> 00:15:35,220
It's not worth it.

320
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:41,937
Anyone worth 30 million berries on his
head is no ordinary man, that's for sure.

321
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:45,077
Hoppa, you can beat him,
you're the strongest man ever!

322
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,042
And you're not afraid of anyone.

323
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:49,477
Darling, I don't have to prove anything.

324
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:52,437
I just need to get by with
enough to keep us happy.

325
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:57,017
So long as you think I'm the greatest,
that's all that matters to me, understand?

326
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,860
Hoppa I scared him off just like that?

327
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:02,557
I guess I don't know how
truly terrifying I am?

328
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,920
Time to flex!

329
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:06,477
I'm glad you came to your senses fool.

330
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:11,089
Now give me my goggles and just maybe
I'll let you escape with your life Huh?

331
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,310
Don't worry.

332
00:16:12,393 --> 00:16:13,377
I'm gonna pay for them.

333
00:16:13,460 --> 00:16:14,637
I'm a killer not a thief.

334
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:17,820
Now give them here He's
letting you go old man.

335
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:20,313
If I were you I'd be running for my life

336
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:22,420
Okay, fine.

337
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:24,797
If that's how you want
it then let's settle

338
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:27,960
this dispute like gentlemen gentlemen here

339
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:30,110
A duel?

340
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:32,240
Yeah, I think I can manage that.

341
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:34,840
If you win, then the goggles are yours.

342
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,300
Two, three, four, six, 30 pistols!

343
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:44,100
That's the same number of
guns as Daddy the Father!

344
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:45,590
It's Daddy the Father!

345
00:16:45,673 --> 00:16:46,717
There's gonna be a duel!

346
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,153
Who can be that stupid?

347
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:50,740
Daddy the Father?

348
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:54,717
Everybody knows that
Daddy the Father is the

349
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:57,137
greatest gunslinger in
bounty hunter history.

350
00:16:57,220 --> 00:17:00,040
Not to mention he's
never lost a duel before.

351
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,220
So what kind of idiot...

352
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:07,440
Oh, that kind.

353
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,860
Good luck, Long Nose.

354
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,706
We got a whole duck for
you already, so relax.

355
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,700
What the hell just happened?

356
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:18,660
Why am I dueling this guy?

357
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:20,340
Simple rules.

358
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,020
Walk ten paces and fire. Okay.

359
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:25,317
What the hell are you doing? Nami!

360
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:28,097
It looks like you're facing
Daddy the Father in a duel!

361
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:29,020
Are you nuts?

362
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:30,177
You're not helping!

363
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:32,277
You never have anything nice to say!

364
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,520
You get one shot!

365
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:34,720
Are you ready?

366
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:46,110
One!

367
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:48,650
Two!

368
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:50,170
Three!

369
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:52,690
Four!

370
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:54,850
Five!

371
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,740
What am I doing? This sucks!

372
00:17:57,940 --> 00:18:00,980
I'm so stupid, there's
no way I can beat him!

373
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:02,640
And six?

374
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,460
I'm gonna die now.

375
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,092
This can't be happening.

376
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:08,630
Seven?

377
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:10,820
I can't believe it.

378
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:14,380
My adventure is just beginning
and I'm already gonna die.

379
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:17,052
Who'd have thought it would come to this?

380
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:18,450
Eight?

381
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:21,790
Ow!

382
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:23,670
Oh!

383
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:39,660
Papa, that was awesome!

384
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:40,901
You're the best!

385
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:42,560
That was just pathetic.

386
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:43,840
What a loser.

387
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:47,788
I don't think I've ever seen
such a cowardly move in my life.

388
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:49,993
What were you thinking?

389
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:50,950
Have you no shame?

390
00:18:51,033 --> 00:18:52,508
I'm cheating during a duel.

391
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,777
You should be ashamed of
yourself, it's pathetic.

392
00:18:54,860 --> 00:18:56,331
I'm so sorry, forgive me.

393
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:58,737
I'm just really too
scared to die this young.

394
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:01,097
Killing me would be too
easy for you, right?

395
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,840
So please don't shoot me.

396
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:05,954
You could just let me go, couldn't you?

397
00:19:07,660 --> 00:19:08,540
No, wait.

398
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,882
Nami, if you want money, my friend
here has tons she can give you.

399
00:19:13,260 --> 00:19:17,200
Please spare me, I'm begging
you, sir. What the hell?

400
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:20,060
So, now you're cowering behind a woman.

401
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:22,070
Listen.

402
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,920
No, leave her out of this.

403
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,437
She has nothing to do with it.

404
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:30,077
I'm the one that got myself into this
situation, and nobody can get me out of it.

405
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,140
It's all on me.

406
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:32,570
Usopp.

407
00:19:32,653 --> 00:19:34,220
Please, just leave Nami out of it.

408
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:35,350
Usopp?

409
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:38,280
Did she just call you Usopp? Yes.

410
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:40,250
Can't be.

411
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:42,937
You wouldn't by any chance know a man by

412
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:45,677
the name of Yasopp of
the Red-Haired Pirates,

413
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:46,940
would you? Yasopp?

414
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:48,560
That's my dad's name.

415
00:19:49,420 --> 00:19:52,714
Wait, are you saying that you
and my father are friends?

416
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:55,000
So then you are his son.

417
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:57,190
Papa?

418
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:59,000
I met your dad,

419
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:03,540
and I've never spoken a single word
to anyone about that fateful day.

420
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:05,180
Until now, that is.

421
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:11,360
We met in a hot, dry port of call
on a day very much like today.

422
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:13,289
Come on, Ensign Masterson.

423
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:14,660
One shot each.

424
00:20:16,020 --> 00:20:18,660
One, two, three...

425
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:34,300
Please, finish me off.

426
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,812
There's no reason for me to live anymore.

427
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:42,360
What are you doing?

428
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:43,620
Your daughter?

429
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,490
Give it.

430
00:20:45,573 --> 00:20:47,537
I wouldn't expect a
cold-blooded marine like

431
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:49,717
yourself to be treasuring
something like this.

432
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,377
Guess she must be really special.

433
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:54,080
And what would a dirty
pirate know about it?

434
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:55,380
Not much.

435
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:59,260
You were awesome, Yasopp.

436
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:00,460
No, I wasn't.

437
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:02,457
I wounded him instead of killing him.

438
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:03,957
Still need more practice.

439
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:06,237
Maybe, but the rest of us
would have been killed.

440
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:08,555
You took on Daddy Masterson and lived!

441
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:13,050
Thanks, boss.

442
00:21:13,133 --> 00:21:17,413
Really, I'm glad you let me duel him
instead of just killing him on sight.

443
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:24,060
It hits the spot.

444
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:26,200
Hey, you want some marine?

445
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,030
Family, huh?

446
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:33,929
I could never wrap my
mind around that job.

447
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:35,500
Is that so?

448
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:37,560
You know, I've got a son.

449
00:21:37,980 --> 00:21:39,360
His name is Usopp.

450
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:40,937
Haven't seen him in years, though.

451
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:47,540
I left him for the sea just when he
started walking why didn't you love him?

452
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:53,037
it wasn't that I loved him
plenty it's just that I loved

453
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:57,940
something else more the sea
was calling for me amen brother

454
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:06,380
Now then,

455
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:12,880
it may be too late for me to do anything
for my son, and I truly regret that.

456
00:22:14,420 --> 00:22:19,300
But you, your daughter, she deserves
to have a parent with her by her side.

457
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:22,197
Don't ever let her go
while you have the chance.

458
00:22:22,280 --> 00:22:23,986
Not that I'm the one to talk.

459
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:30,840
I lost our duel, Yasum!

460
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,757
You can't leave me here like this!

461
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,380
You owe that much to me!

462
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:38,777
You Marines may have to follow the
rules and do everything by the book,

463
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:42,277
but the best part about being a pirate
is that I can do whatever I want,

464
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:43,380
whenever I want.

465
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:44,750
Later.

466
00:22:59,100 --> 00:22:59,980
Papa, no!

467
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:01,997
A pirate didn't spare your life!

468
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:03,374
Tell me it's not true!

469
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:04,880
Usopp? Wow!

470
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:06,957
Your father must have been amazing!

471
00:23:07,040 --> 00:23:10,200
He beat Daddy the Father! Usopp? I get it!

472
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:13,597
I understand why you tell me
that story about my father!

473
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:16,739
You told me that so I would
try to be more like him!

474
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:18,070
Huh?

475
00:23:18,153 --> 00:23:19,782
You embarrassed yourself for me!

476
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:23,557
You put yourself beneath me so I would
know what type of man my father was!

477
00:23:23,640 --> 00:23:24,817
I'll never forget that!

478
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:28,841
Most people would just bury that
story and never tell it to anyone.

479
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:33,040
But you, you're not afraid
of anything, even shame.

480
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:36,480
A coward would never do what you just did.

481
00:23:38,100 --> 00:23:40,800
Carol, your dad is the bravest man alive.

482
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:43,557
Men who are big and
strong are easy to find,

483
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:48,169
but the ones who put their honor on the
line for others are one in a million.

484
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:50,640
I can't.

485
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:54,137
If I accept your dad's mercy,
it'll only bring him more shame.

486
00:23:54,220 --> 00:23:57,044
I have one choice, and
that is to face my death.

487
00:23:57,300 --> 00:23:58,653
Give me another chance.

488
00:23:58,900 --> 00:24:01,782
I have to prove to myself
that I am not a coward.

489
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,500
A life or death fight.

490
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:09,960
All right.

491
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:12,857
Choose the weapon you feel
most comfortable with.

492
00:24:12,940 --> 00:24:14,587
This will be our final duel.

493
00:24:18,100 --> 00:24:18,930
Good.

494
00:24:19,013 --> 00:24:21,860
Now, let's see.

495
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:28,460
You must hit that
weather vane. What? That?

496
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,320
If you miss.

497
00:24:33,860 --> 00:24:34,690
Right.

498
00:24:34,773 --> 00:24:36,740
You'll shoot me through the heart.

499
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:38,270
Usopp?

500
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:42,073
So this shot determines whether
I live or die with honor.

501
00:24:46,780 --> 00:24:47,900
He can't.

502
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:51,236
There's no way he can shoot
that far with a slingshot.

503
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:13,420
You've missed.

504
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:15,347
Please don't kill him, Papa.

505
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:16,300
Please, no.

506
00:25:18,380 --> 00:25:21,792
I can't shoot him because he
shot right through the crown.

507
00:25:24,220 --> 00:25:26,120
He did it, Usopp! He's right!

508
00:25:26,980 --> 00:25:28,000
Good job!

509
00:25:28,420 --> 00:25:32,126
You're as good a shot as your
old man, and a brave one as well.

510
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:33,960
Your father will be proud.

511
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:35,620
Go to the Grand Line.

512
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:37,400
You'll find him there.

513
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:42,780
He deserves to see what
his son has become.

514
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:44,250
Daddy.

515
00:25:46,660 --> 00:25:49,000
You're a pretty good shot, old man.

516
00:25:49,620 --> 00:25:50,450
Thanks.

517
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:52,150
Later!

518
00:25:52,660 --> 00:25:53,880
Wait, Papa!

519
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:56,780
Now, Carol, don't say later.

520
00:25:57,060 --> 00:25:58,580
It's bad manners.

521
00:25:59,660 --> 00:26:00,840
Sorry, Papa.

522
00:26:01,220 --> 00:26:04,320
I'm gonna try to be a nice
little girl from now on.

523
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:07,280
My little age, you're nice enough.

524
00:26:08,380 --> 00:26:10,557
Well, I'm gonna be even nicer.

525
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:13,875
When people say Daddy the
Father is a disgraced Marine,

526
